! Queensland-style ISOLATED Single-Wire Earth-Return (SWER) feeder.
! Power-flow comparison / analysis test case.
!
! ============================================================================
! Topology (small canonical isolated-SWER feeder)
! ============================================================================
!
!     22 kV 3-phase                         12.7 kV SWER (single wire + earth)
!  src --3ph-- mv --[iso xfmr]-- swer_0 --line-- swer_1 --line-- swer_2
!  (slack)      |  1-ph 12.7/12.7            |                     |
!               |  earth confined to SWER  [dx1: 25 kVA       [dx2: 10 kVA
!         (MV neutral earthed)               single-ended       split-phase
!                                            N-0]               centre-tap N-0-N]
!                                              |                    |
!                                            lv_1 (0.24 kV)      lv_2 (0.48 kV, 0-N-0)
!                                            1-ph load           two 0.24 kV legs
!
! "Isolated" SWER: a dedicated 1:1 isolating transformer galvanically separates
! the SWER line from the three-phase MV feeder, so the earth-return current is
! confined to the SWER system (cf. Nobbs, "Development of advanced SWER models
! for the Ergon Energy network", UniSQ 2012 — isolated/unisolated/duplex/triplex
! taxonomy; this is the isolated case). Downstream the zone is a single-phase,
! transformer-isolated galvanic island, which BMOPF classifies as :swer.
!
! ============================================================================
! Queensland (Ergon) design parameters
! ============================================================================
!   MV feeder            22 kV line-line, 3-phase
!   SWER voltage         12.7 kV phase-earth (= 22 kV / sqrt(3))
!   Isolating xfmr       <= 300 kVA, 12.7 kV (across one MV phase-earth) -> 12.7 kV SWER
!   Distribution xfmrs   25 kVA single-ended N-0; 10 kVA split-phase N-0-N
!   LV utilisation       0.24 kV single-ended; 0.48 kV centre-tapped (240-0-240)
!   Load density         < 0.5 kVA/km; single customer < 3.5 kVA
! Refs: ScienceDirect, "Rural SWER distribution networks - associated problems
!   and cost-effective solutions", IJEPES 2011; Ergon Distribution Annual
!   Planning Report.
!
! ============================================================================
! Protection context (documentation only - BMOPF does not model protection)
! ============================================================================
!   A SWER spur tapped off a 3-phase main draws current on a single phase; a
!   fault on the spur appears as an imbalance (overcurrent on the affected
!   phases) detectable by Negative-Phase-Sequence (NPS) protection on the
!   mainline recloser, allowing it to grade with the single-phase spur. Earth-
!   fault protection is especially important because the load return path is the
!   earth itself.  Refs: NOJA Power, "Electricity Distribution using Two Wire
!   Single Phase" and "How to protect Two Pole Single Phase Overhead Lines with
!   Reclosers".
! ============================================================================

Clear

! Base frequency locked to 50 Hz (BMOPF's modelling frequency).  The OpenDSS
! default (60 Hz, or whatever a Windows GUI session persisted) would otherwise
! rescale every reactance.  See docs/src/validation.md.
Set DefaultBaseFreq=50

! The 3-phase ideal source perfectly grounds its own star point, so no explicit
! MV neutral-earth reactor is needed.
New Circuit.qld_swer basekv=22.0 pu=1.0 angle=0 phases=3 bus1=mv.1.2.3 model=ideal

Redirect Linecodes.dss
Redirect Lines.dss
Redirect Transformers.dss
Redirect Groundings.dss
Redirect Loads.dss

! OpenDSS VoltageBases are LINE-TO-LINE, so each entry is divided by sqrt(3) to
! get a bus's phase-to-earth kVBase.  22.0 therefore covers both the 3-phase MV
! bus and the 12.7 kV SWER buses (12.7 = 22/sqrt(3)) -- a listed 12.7 would be
! redundant.  The LV entry must likewise be the sqrt(3)-scaled 0.24 kV:  entering
! 0.24 directly bases the LV buses at 0.1386 kV and reports nominal 240 V as
! 1.723 pu.
Set VoltageBases=[22.0, 0.41569]
CalcVoltageBases
! Tolerance 1e-8 (<< the voltage-comparison tolerance) removes OpenDSS-side
! convergence slop; MaxIterations raised so the tighter target is reached.
Set Tolerance=1e-8
Set MaxIterations=100
Solve
